.TH KULAN-WELCOME 1 "November 2026" "Kulan OS" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kulan-welcome \- Kulan OS Setup Assistant
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kulan-welcome
[\fB\-\-autostart\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kulan-welcome
opens the Kulan OS Setup Assistant: get online (Wi-Fi, when the computer
isn't connected), choose light or dark mode and an accent colour, install
popular apps from Flathub in one go (only apps that run on this computer are
offered; the list fills in by itself once online), download Ask Kulan's
model when the assistant is installed, and see which security protections
are on.
.PP
It opens automatically the first time you sign in, and never in the live session. It is
marked done when it's finished; closed early, it opens once more the next time
you sign in, and then not again. It can be reopened at any time from the app grid.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-autostart
Exit straight away if Setup is done for this user or if running in the
live session. Used by the sign-in autostart entry.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/kulan-welcome/done
Created when Setup is finished (or after it has opened twice); delete it
to see Setup the next time you sign in. The autostart entry checks it too
(AutostartCondition), so nothing starts once it exists.
.TP
.I ~/.config/kulan-welcome/reminded
Setup opened at sign-in but wasn't finished: it opens once more.
.TP
.I /usr/share/kulan/kulan.conf
Product name and website shown in Setup.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR flatpak (1),
.BR ufw (8)
